I always, you know, thought like, okay,

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.530
I'm gonna meet love my
life in high school.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.230
Head in the clouds, you know.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.417
(giggles)

00:00:22.417 --> 00:00:25.000
(techno music)

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.030
- [Director] It was love at first sight.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:35.835
Three, two, one.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:38.668
(heavy breathing)

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.703
(giggles)

00:00:45.703 --> 00:00:49.110
- I saw him in a grocery
store when I was 15.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.300
- I saw her and she was
a, you know, a customer

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.329
and I was a stock boy,
and so I stalked her.

00:00:54.329 --> 00:00:55.890
(laughing)

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.080
Aisle eight, the cheese aisle.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.839
So yeah, I totally fell in love with her.

00:01:00.839 --> 00:01:01.672
- [Participant] Beautiful.

00:01:01.672 --> 00:01:04.170
- The whole entire school
year I sat right next to him,

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.240
and I didn't say not one word to him.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.950
One of the last days of school,

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:11.220
we were just doing our work
and he started singing.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.490
So I actually fell in love with his voice

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.980
before anything. (giggles)

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:19.386
- It takes us two years
for us to start dating.

00:01:19.386 --> 00:01:20.219
- Mmhmm.

00:01:20.219 --> 00:01:23.100
- We've known each other for
so long, since second grade.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.070
I mean, I had several crushes
on her, like, growing up.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.920
- Fifth grade, I remember I
really had a crush on him,

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.260
but then my attraction towards him, like,

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:33.030
wavered throughout the years.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.520
But I think it was more of
like a feeling that, like,

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:37.820
the feeling of love towards him was like,

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.780
kind of always there.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:43.410
- For us, we were 15
sophomore year of high school.

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.480
We sat in like, diagonals.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.280
We would like, always look
at each other and make

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.810
eye contact from across the room,

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:51.390
but nobody like, pursued anything.

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:53.160
So that's why I kind of went to somewhat

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:54.540
'cause it was always there

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.003
but we didn't actually
act on it until later on.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.987
- [Director] I said, I love you first.

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:05.987
Three, two, one.

00:02:09.358 --> 00:02:12.088
- It was 30 years ago, you
don't remember? (laughs)

00:02:12.088 --> 00:02:13.728
- Yep, I said it.

00:02:13.728 --> 00:02:14.583
(laughing)

00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:16.110
Yep, and then she said it right after.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.797
So, I said it first.

00:02:17.797 --> 00:02:19.650
- It caught me off guard, honestly.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:20.760
Like, it was like, what?

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:23.340
Oh, I love you too. (laughs)

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:25.080
- I definitely said it first.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.810
And then I remember, I was like,

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:29.106
did you hear what I just said?

00:02:29.106 --> 00:02:31.294
(laughs)
(gasps)

00:02:31.294 --> 00:02:32.127
Cause she didn't say anything at all.

00:02:32.127 --> 00:02:33.150
I was like, oh no.

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.265
And then you were like,
yeah, I love you too.

00:02:35.265 --> 00:02:36.098
(laughs)

00:02:36.098 --> 00:02:39.780
- I think I loved her first,
but I didn't say it first.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.250
I think she said it first.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:44.190
- I probably did, but
I just don't remember.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:45.878
- I'm more reserved,
- The moment.

00:02:45.878 --> 00:02:46.874
so I wouldn't have said it first.

00:02:46.874 --> 00:02:48.150
(laughs)

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.913
- [Director] You're never
too young to fall in love.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.553
Three, two, one.

00:02:56.378 --> 00:02:58.378
(sighs)

00:03:03.027 --> 00:03:04.405
- Somewhat agree.

00:03:04.405 --> 00:03:05.370
- Too young is like, I
don't know, five, six.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.473
Before you really
(giggling)

00:03:07.473 --> 00:03:08.726
understand what love is.

00:03:08.726 --> 00:03:11.760
But once you're like, old
enough to start thinking

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:15.540
about having a boyfriend,
girlfriend situation like,

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:18.840
I think then you start to
understand what love is

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:22.170
and that feeling that you
get inside your chest.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.481
- I agree, so I'm gonna move over here.

00:03:24.481 --> 00:03:25.314
(giggling)

00:03:25.314 --> 00:03:26.760
I feel like the reason I was there was

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.860
because I was thinking like super young,

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.190
but obviously no six year old's gonna be

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.030
falling in love. (laughs)

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:34.455
- Yes.

00:03:34.455 --> 00:03:36.810
- But I feel like for me,
one of the struggles has been

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:39.060
like, losing the stigma of like,

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.560
being too young to be in love.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:42.270
Where people are like, oh, you don't know.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.530
Like, you don't really know.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.287
But I feel like it's a
feeling and you feel it,

00:03:45.287 --> 00:03:46.950
and it doesn't matter how old you are.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.420
If you met the person
that you're in love with

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.640
then you're in love with that person.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:51.960
- [Director] I always saw myself

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.510
marrying my high school sweetheart.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.387
Three.

00:03:56.387 --> 00:03:58.320
Three, two, one.

00:04:03.313 --> 00:04:05.533
- I grew up on Disney.

00:04:05.533 --> 00:04:07.886
(laughing)

00:04:07.886 --> 00:04:11.085
I always, you know, thought like, okay,

00:04:11.085 --> 00:04:12.720
I'm gonna meet the love
of my life in high school.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:15.570
Head in the clouds, you know? (laughs)

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:16.403
- Yeah, I agree.

00:04:16.403 --> 00:04:17.700
I'm a romantic.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:21.180
So I always wanted to marry
like, my high school sweetheart.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:22.013
I was always like,

00:04:22.013 --> 00:04:24.180
I hope I fall in love
young and meet somebody.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.310
And then I was lucky
enough to have it happen.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:28.920
- My parents taught me growing
up, they had always said,

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.320
you know, like, make
yourself established first.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:32.153
Get a job.

00:04:32.153 --> 00:04:33.060
And then you can find somebody.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:36.210
So, I think that's kind of why I'm here,

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.310
right here in the, in the disagree.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:42.480
- I just distinctly remember
like, conversations with her.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:44.190
I wanna marry you, blah, blah, blah.

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:46.920
Like, not really understanding
the weight of that.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.930
But at the same time, it's like,

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:52.470
when you have something so
perfect right in front of you,

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:55.650
why would you mess with anything else?

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:58.233
- All of my family, they
all met in high school,

00:04:58.233 --> 00:05:00.270
and married their high school sweethearts,

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:01.920
so it wasn't that it was foreign to me.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.740
But I knew when I met him, when I would

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:07.740
write his name on my
peachy folder (laughs)

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.510
that's when it kind of came alive for me.

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:11.640
- I didn't think I would be married at 21,

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.290
which is a really young age.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:14.220
Plans change.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:15.720
And we decided that we were

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.990
gonna get married at 21 and she was 19.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:21.030
- I mean like boys in high
school were always like,

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:22.830
not the best, you know?

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.233
Like, it was just like,
just young, we're so young.

00:05:25.233 --> 00:05:27.420
Like I was like, am I
gonna marry this guy?

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:28.380
Like, I don't know.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:30.960
When I was in high school I
did have that feeling like,

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:32.250
I was, I'm gonna marry him.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.080
Like, even though we weren't
together, I was like,

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.420
I have a feeling like at the end of this

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:38.400
like, I was gonna marry him.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.233
We're not married yet.

00:05:39.233 --> 00:05:40.983
But eventually.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:45.060
- [Director] There was a time
in the past where I thought

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:47.340
we might break up.

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:49.983
Three, two, one.

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:01.383
- Being in a relationship for a long time,

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:05.790
everyone gets in fights and
that's like a healthy and

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:07.320
kind of negative part of a relationship.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:10.290
But, personally I view
fights and arguments

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:13.590
as kind of like building together with us.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:16.020
Like, yeah, there were
times where we had, you know

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:17.880
pretty heavy arguments,
but I think deep down

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.950
I knew that we were still
gonna make it together.

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:21.450
- I feel like we went from being

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:23.010
children to being adults together.

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:24.300
Obviously there's gonna be problems,

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.520
you have to figure that out along the way.

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:29.850
And I think that being at the
breaking point, being like,

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:31.140
I don't know if I can do this anymore,

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.630
but then still choosing
to be together is what

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:35.288
makes you strong and is what makes you

00:06:35.288 --> 00:06:37.620
realize like, this is the person.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.510
Because a lot of people tend to give up

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:41.220
but I never wanted to give up.

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:43.833
And I was like, no, like,
I want him and only him.

00:06:45.982 --> 00:06:47.011
- Why are you standing over there?

00:06:47.011 --> 00:06:48.763
(giggles)

00:06:48.763 --> 00:06:51.240
- I would always say like, I
had so much growing up to do

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:54.000
when I was younger, just
like, mental health wise

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.540
and just everything that,
at this felt like I was a

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:01.789
burden to you or that I was
like, causing you a lot of pain.

00:07:01.789 --> 00:07:03.600
Oh my God, I don't wanna cry.

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:06.930
But, you know, like, just being a

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:08.940
negative energy in your sphere.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:10.740
So I thought, you know, it's better for me

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:13.020
just not to be with you
so you could be happier.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:14.550
But then I stuck it
through, you stuck through,

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:15.643
that's the amazing part.

00:07:15.643 --> 00:07:17.843
It was like, you stuck
through and you like,

00:07:19.221 --> 00:07:20.220
even through all my ups and
downs you're always there

00:07:21.079 --> 00:07:22.530
to get me through it and
just were always there.

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:23.670
Even though I was just like,

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:26.370
could be really mean or
could be very negative,

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:28.170
but now we're in a better
place where you've like,

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:30.210
taught me how to grow and stuff.

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:32.370
So that's why I was like,
strongly agree, 'cause I,

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:34.170
not because it was never anything you did,

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:36.120
it was more for me to like, find myself

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:39.090
and not have to hurt you in the process.

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:41.730
- I mean, for our first
year it was, it was rough.

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:45.780
Like, we were just like,
ships passing in the night.

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:49.350
I mean, he was full-time
working, full-time in college.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:51.360
I was going to school and working.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:54.540
And the challenges of being,
you know, young, new parents.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:57.060
And it was just, it, it
was a rough first year.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:00.510
And I think there was a point
where we both, I, I think

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:02.940
that we both kind of thought
like, are we gonna make this?

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:06.330
- There was one distinct
night where we fought so bad

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:09.229
because I mean, it was
just a boiling point where

00:08:09.229 --> 00:08:14.229
our first son, I had his right
hand, she had his left hand,

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:17.970
and we were tugging at him.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.470
He's going with me.

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:23.040
No, he's going with me,
but we didn't wanna leave

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.900
because we wanted to be with our son.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:26.061
- Yeah.

00:08:26.061 --> 00:08:27.390
- So that night we actually stayed.

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:29.730
And that was like a
defining moment where like,

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:31.890
okay we're gonna work this out because we

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:33.783
have to work it out for our family.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.440
- [Director] Building a family is an

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:40.353
important part of our relationship to me.

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:44.010
Three, two, one.

00:08:49.843 --> 00:08:52.620
- I mean, for me, this is a no brainer.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:55.080
I mean, growing up, I always
had this dream of like,

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:56.703
I'm gonna have this big family.

00:08:59.365 --> 00:09:01.350
And it's almost like, I just
feel I'm living out this dream.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:02.880
I mean, I know it sounds so simple,

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:05.340
but it is literally having children.

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:09.330
I mean, we've had a, we've
had a lot of losses also.

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:10.163
Sorry.

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:14.147
Yeah.

00:09:14.147 --> 00:09:15.090
We've had four children here.

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:16.263
We have four in heaven.

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:21.840
And for us it was never
easy to get pregnant.

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:24.160
And when we did, it was such a gift.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.440
(choking up)

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:28.020
Sorry, I don't mean to be so emotional.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:32.760
But, my kids, my grandkids,
now we have a daughter-in-law.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:35.610
I mean, it literally
makes my heart so happy

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:38.580
when I see them, when they
walk through the door.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.370
I mean, I feel like those are
some of our happiest times

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:44.100
just when our children and
our family is all together.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:46.170
It's just, it's amazing.

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:47.003
- Yeah.

00:09:47.003 --> 00:09:49.980
- That is truly inspiring in so many ways.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:53.490
Like, I truly wanna be like,
you wanna grow up. (laughs)

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:56.310
Right now at the moment,
like, you are my family.

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:57.453
- Oh yeah.

00:09:57.453 --> 00:09:58.689
- I've always had a big family.

00:09:58.689 --> 00:09:59.522
- Yeah.

00:09:59.522 --> 00:10:01.860
- So that's something that
I've always inspired to have,

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:03.660
and I couldn't imagine doing that

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.670
with anyone else besides you.

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:06.503
- Me as well.

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:10.590
- The reason I feel like
we love each other so much

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:13.050
and stay together is
'cause we have envisioned

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:17.190
a future of building a family,
having a healthy household.

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:18.023
- Yeah.

00:10:18.023 --> 00:10:20.490
We wanna be able to
cultivate an environment

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:21.930
and see how we do as parents.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:24.870
I think that's what's so exciting
about our future is like,

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:28.276
how do we break any generational
curses and all that stuff.

00:10:28.276 --> 00:10:29.109
- Yes!

00:10:29.109 --> 00:10:29.942
- Yeah.

00:10:29.942 --> 00:10:34.140
And just, you know, become
the parents that have

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:36.720
really healthy relationships
with their kids,

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:40.290
and so that's what I'm super
excited for in the future.

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:42.540
- Obviously, we live
with our family so our

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:44.880
family relationship is based on them,

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:47.190
but I wanna build one with you.

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:50.070
And like, obviously like, how could,

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:50.970
I'm so in love with him, like,

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:52.653
how could I not wanna have a kid with him?

00:10:52.653 --> 00:10:55.380
So like I want have family.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:57.240
Have my kids names picked out already.

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:59.100
Like, I've been there. (laughs)

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:00.330
- And have our own identity.

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:01.163
- Yeah.

00:11:02.742 --> 00:11:06.450
- [Director] This is my favorite
time in our relationship.

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:08.730
Three, two, one.

00:11:18.591 --> 00:11:21.570
- We recently went through a rough patch.

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:23.400
We're like, on the up now,

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:26.460
but I feel like, we're
still there kind of.

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:27.870
We're still trying to work through it.

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:29.640
So I feel like we've had better moments

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:32.070
but I'm glad that it did happen
because now it's only gonna

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:34.680
make us stronger and we're
only gonna go up from here.

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:38.160
- Yeah, and I'm gonna go with
just the cliche answer that

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:40.830
you know, every moment is
my favorite moment with her

00:11:40.830 --> 00:11:44.190
regardless of whether we're
mad at each other, happy.

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:46.320
It's just always my favorite.

